# Fathom - water and weather.
#
# Most of the sound of water is bubbles: air caught under the surface rings
# at a pitch set by its size and rises as it nears the top. A drip is a
# bubble and a tap; rain is many drips and what they land on; a stream is a
# cloud of small bubbles and a few big ones; surf is a wave's rush. Wind is
# air rushing past, in gusts, whistling where it's caught; fire is
# crackles, hiss and roar.
#
# A held note keeps it going: the note sets the bubbles' size or the
# wind's whistle, the velocity how much. `density` is how many events,
# `size` how far their pitches spread, `rise` how far a bubble climbs,
# `decay` how long each rings, `surface` what the rain falls on, `gust` how
# much the wind, fire and waves come and go, `whistle` the wind caught in a
# gap, `tone` how bright, `swell` beats from wave to wave, `fade` how long
# it takes to come and go. Pressure and the mod wheel thicken it.
#
# Ninety patches in eight families, plainest first:
#
#   water    Init, bubbles, drips and below the surface (13)
#   stream   brooks, rivers, waterfalls and splashes (12)
#   sea      surf, shore and swells (9)
#   rain     rain, hail and rainsticks (14)
#   weather  wind and thunder (12)
#   fire     fires, pans and steam (10)
#   winter   snow, ice, sleet and blizzards (10)
#   kit      sixteen pads each: a scene on one track (10)
#
# Bubble Notes, Drip Notes, Bubble Melody, Whistling Wind, Moaning Wind and
# Wind Whistle play the note, for tunes on the keys. The far patches (Distant
# River, Far Surf, Sea Cave, Distant Rain, Rolling Thunder, Frozen Lake and
# Cave Kit) carry a reverb send; Near Surf is dry and wide.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are
# numbered as in Fathom.h's MacroDest: #1 density, #2 size, #3 rise, #4
# decay, #5 gust, #6 whistle, #7 tone, #8 swell, #9 spread, #10 fade, #12
# volume, #13 pitch (24 semitones a unit). Each sound gets the eight that
# move it: bubbles More, Bigger, Rise, Ring, Deep, High, Wide and Calm;
# surf Foam, Waves, Bright, Dark, Long, Quick, Bigger and Still; wind
# Gusts, Lull, Whistle, Bright, Dark, Low, High and Slow; and so on for
# rain, hail, thunder, fire, ice and snow. A kit's macros reach the knobs
# every pad shares, and More and Calm each pad's own density too. Where a
# macro at full moves the level by more than 1.5 dB, a volume route takes it
# back out, and where the volume is already near the top the macro goes less
# far. Levels are read off a held note, since a 2 s note of sparse drops or
# slow gusts can land anywhere.

machine Fathom
role pad

# --- water --------------------------------------------------------------------

patch Init family=water note=48 range=36..60

patch "Fish Tank" family=water note=55 range=43..67
  # A steady line of small bubbles.
  set macro1 "More"
  set macro2 "Bigger"
  set macro3 "Rise"
  set macro4 "Ring"
  set macro5 "Deep"
  set macro6 "High"
  set macro7 "Wide"
  set macro8 "Calm"
  mac1_d1  #1
  mac1_a1  0.35
  mac1_d2  #12
  mac1_a2  -0.353
  mac2_d1  #2
  mac2_a1  0.3
  mac3_d1  #3
  mac3_a1  0.5
  mac4_d1  #4
  mac4_a1  0.4
  mac4_d2  #12
  mac4_a2  -0.138
  mac5_d1  #13
